{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MassIdentityUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MassIdentityUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassIdentity.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassIdentity.unique","kind":"theorem","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-unique.lean#L20-L33","doc":"**Uniqueness of the inertial mass identity.**\n\nFor a fixed Frobenius form `∫_A`, two mass values computed via\n`scalarMass` on the same closed cycle coincide — uniqueness up\nto the scalar ambiguity of `∫_A` (which is itself unique up to\nscalar by Frobenius-pairing uniqueness).  Encoded here as: two\ninputs with the same trace produce the same norm. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mass-identity-unique","label":"prop:mass-identity-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}